# Clayify asks each visitor for their own PicX key through the gear in the header,
# so no server-side key is required. Leaving PICX_API_KEY unset is the intended
# setup — it means the app can never spend one key on another visitor's request.
#
# Set it only if you want the server to carry its own key locally. A key supplied
# in the browser always wins over it.
# PICX_API_KEY=pxsk_your_key_here

# Demo escape hatch, leave unset in any real deployment.
#
# `images.edit` reads public URLs, and uploading a local file to PicX needs the
# "Upload files" (uploads:write) scope. If a key lacks it, setting this uploads
# the photo to a public third-party file host instead so the app still works.
#
# The photo then leaves your control: it sits on a public host at an
# unauthenticated URL and is not deleted automatically.
# CLAY_UPLOAD_FALLBACK=catbox
